desc(
	mode: "source"
	language: "general"
	title: "Dml Native Statements"
	title_zh: "检测到Dml Native Statements",
	type: vuln
	level: middle
	rule_id: "source-insecure-api-dml-native-statements"
	risk: "Security"
	desc: <<<DESC
Migrated from Semgrep rule `dml-native-statements` (/tmp/semgrep-rules/apex/lang/security/ncino/dml/DmlNativeStatements.yaml).
Original message: Native Salesforce DML operations execute in system context, ignoring the current user's permissions, field-level security, organization-wide defaults, position in the role hierarchy, and sharing rules. Be mindful when using native Salesforce DML operations.

CWE: CWE-863: Incorrect Authorization
References:
- https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.apexref.meta/apexref/apex_dml_section.htm
- https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/863.html
- https://owasp.org/Top10/A04_2021-Insecure_Design/
DESC
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
Review the flagged code and follow the framework's secure coding guidance: use safe APIs, escape output, and avoid hardcoded credentials.
SOLUTION
	alert_min: 1
	"file://pos.cls": <<<POS
update

POS
	"safefile://neg.sample": <<<NEG
# safe sample
no secrets here
just regular code
NEG
)

${*.cls}.pattern_regex_not(/(insert|upsert|update|delete)[\s]/, /[\/\/].*(insert|upsert|update|delete).*/, /[\/\/].*(insert|upsert|update|delete)[\n]/, /.*[=].*(insert|upsert|update|delete).*[,;]/) as $p0
${*.cls}.pattern_regex_not(/(insert|upsert|update|delete)[(]/, /[\/\/].*(insert|upsert|update|delete).*/, /[\/\/].*(insert|upsert|update|delete)[\n]/, /.*[=].*(insert|upsert|update|delete).*[,;]/) as $p1
$p0 + $p1 as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "middle",
	title: "Dml Native Statements",
	title_zh: "检测到Dml Native Statements",
	message: "Dml Native Statements",
}
